++<article class="vuln card" id="CRED-01" data-sev="Critical" data-cat="Credentials" data-search="cred-01 instagram account password persisted on-device in a reversible cipher credentials the private-api login path stores the victim's real instagram password in the room table instagram_accounts , column u_w . the value passed to setu_w() is com.bumptech.glide.d.q(password) a keyless static byte transform, not encryption. any process or backup that can read the app's data directory recovers the password in one line. full instagram account takeover. the password (not just a session) is captured, so an attacker can also reset 2fa, change the e-mail and permanently lock the victim out. every account the user ever adds is exposed. ia.v.a(ia.v,string) v7_1.setu_w(com.bumptech.glide.d.q(v6.getpassword())) ; room ddl instagram_accounts(... `u_w` text ...) never accept or store the user's instagram password. use instagram's official oauth (which this app does not); at absolute minimum store only a short-lived session token in android keystore-backed encryptedsharedpreferences.">
++  <header>
++    <div class="vid">CRED-01</div>
++    <span class="badge" style="--c:#ff3b6b">Critical</span>
++    <span class="cat">Credentials</span>
++  </header>
++  <h3>Instagram account PASSWORD persisted on-device in a reversible cipher</h3>
++  <div class="grid2">
++    <div><h4>How it works</h4><p>The private-API login path stores the victim's real Instagram password in the Room table <code>instagram_accounts</code>, column <code>u_w</code>. The value passed to <code>setU_w()</code> is <code>com.bumptech.glide.d.q(password)</code> &mdash; a keyless static byte transform, not encryption. Any process or backup that can read the app's data directory recovers the password in one line.</p></div>
++    <div><h4>Impact</h4><p>Full Instagram account takeover. The password (not just a session) is captured, so an attacker can also reset 2FA, change the e-mail and permanently lock the victim out. Every account the user ever adds is exposed.</p></div>
