++    <div><h4>How it works</h4><p>The pin literal recovered from <code>libtopfollow.so</code> .rodata is <code>sha256/d845591e086033a9035fd6b66c3c3d73aa33af90794d6b986e64779eea6bec5e</code>. That is byte-for-byte the SHA-256 of the APK's own signing certificate (self-signed, <code>CN=Maryam Ahmadi, OU=Android Developer, O=NivaRoid, L=Shiraz, ST=Fars, C=IR</code>, serial 1, RSA-2048, valid 2023-12-15 &rarr; 2048-12-08). The same digest is also the tamper-check value, so one constant does two unrelated jobs. Worse, the <em>live</em> pin is whatever the server pushed into SharedPreferences <code>Pin</code> / <code>PinActive</code>.</p></div>
